0.8.0: the history release - instant expansion and 1920s-1950s color

Five new cameras (thirteen total). Instant: polaroid-sx70 (earlier
integral chemistry, warmer and dreamier; canonical px-70) and
polaroid-packfilm (peel-apart Land-camera geometry via the per-preset
frame millimeter fields - 83x108 mm outer, thin even border; canonical
polaroid_669 from the newly fetched instant_pro family). Historical:
autochrome (Lumiere plates: pastel palette, soft plate optics, and
pointillist colored grain via the new grain_chroma axis - independent
per-channel noise), midcentury-rangefinder (uncoated-lens flare,
canonical Kodachrome 64), technicolor-3strip (1.375:1 Academy gate,
saturated dye-transfer color).

Engine: grain_chroma preset scalar blends luminance grain toward
independent per-channel noise; trait summaries now print the actual gate
ratio. fetch_luts.sh adds the instant_pro family; the web stages eleven
films with blurbs (PX-70, Time-Zero expired, 669, Kodachrome 64 join).
Tests: chroma-grain channel decorrelation, pack-film geometry, Academy
gate, preset count.
